03-31T15:15:15.153000Z", "modified": "2025-04-02T19:09:11.370000Z", "description": "On BIG-IP versions 16.0.x before 16.0.1.1, 15.1.x before 15.1.2.1, 14.1.x before 14.1.4, 13.1.x before 13.1.3.6, and 12.1.x before 12.1.5.3 amd BIG-IQ 7.1.0.x before 7.1.0.3 and 7.0.0.x before 7.0.0.2, the iControl REST interface has an unauthenticated remote command execution vulnerability. Note: Software versions which have reached End of Software Development (EoSD) are not evaluated.", "cvssV31": {"@type": "CvssV31", "score": 9.8, "severity": "CRITICAL", "vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "metricSource": "nvd@nist.gov", "metricType": "Primary"}, "cvssV2Score": 10.0, "nReferences": 6, "weaknessAssignment": [{"@type": "WeaknessAssignment", "weakness": [{"@id": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/918.html", "@type": "Weakness", "cweId": "CWE-918", "isInformative": true}], "assignedBy": "134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0", "assignmentType": "Secondary"}, {"@type": "WeaknessAssignment", "weakness": [{"@id": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/918.html", "@type": "Weakness", "cweId": "CWE-918", "isInformative": true}], "assignedBy": "nvd@nist.gov", "assignmentType": "Primary"}], "wasDerivedFrom": ["https://github.com/fkie-cad/nvd-json-data-feeds/tree/a4262227a26a698199ea8d287932f8639e85aa6d"]}, "mappings": [{"@id": "urn:threatgraph:pkev-mapping:668", "@type": "Mapping", "mappingType": "exploitation_technique", "capabilityGroup": "code_execution", "comments": "CVE-2021-22986 is a remote command execution vulnerability occurring on the iControl REST interface. Impact reported by the F5 security advisory \"This vulnerability allows for unauthenticated attackers with network access to the iControl REST interface, through the BIG-IP management interface and self IP addresses, to execute arbitrary system commands, create or delete files, and disable services. This vulnerability can only be exploited through the control plane and cannot be exploited through the data plane. Exploitation can lead to complete system compromise. \"", "evidenceUrl": ["https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2021/03/to-security-pros-dread-another-critical-server-vulnerability-is-under-exploit/", "https://my.f5.com/manage/s/article/K03009991", "https://www.cpomagazine.com/cyber-security/massive-cyber-attacks-target-f5-big-ip-critical-vulnerabilities-after-firm-releases-updates/"], "wasDerivedFrom": ["https://github.com/center-for-threat-informed-defense/mappings-explorer/tree/ddc842aa48c871cbfc2219cdbb842e9a4e155afe"], "technique": {"@id": "https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1190/", "@type": "AttackTechnique", "techniqueId": "T1190", "name": "Exploit Public-Facing Application", "tactic": [{"@id": "https://attack.mitre.org/tactics/TA0001/", "@type": "AttackTactic", "tacticId": "TA0001", "shortname": "initial-access"}]}}, {"@id": "urn:threatgraph:pkev-mapping:669", "@type": "Mapping", "mappingType": "secondary_impact", "capabilityGroup": "code_execution", "comments": "CVE-2021-22986 is a remote command execution vulnerability occurring on the iControl REST interface. Impact reported by the F5 security advisory \"This vulnerability allows for unauthenticated attackers with network access to the iControl REST interface, through the BIG-IP management interface and self IP addresses, to execute arbitrary system commands, create or delete files, and disable services. This vulnerability can only be exploited through the control plane and cannot be exploited through the data plane. Exploitation can lead to complete system compromise. \"", "evidenceUrl": ["https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2021/03/to-security-pros-dread-another-critical-server-vulnerability-is-under-exploit/", "https://my.f5.com/manage/s/article/K03009991", "https://www.cpomagazine.com/cyber-security/massive-cyber-attacks-target-f5-big-ip-critical-vulnerabilities-after-firm-releases-updates/"], "wasDerivedFrom": ["https://github.com/center-for-threat-informed-defense/mappings-explorer/tree/ddc84