ote attackers to download arbitrary files from the SimpleHelp host via crafted HTTP requests. These files include server configuration files containing various secrets and hashed user passwords.", "cvssV31": {"@type": "CvssV31", "score": 7.5, "severity": "HIGH", "vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N", "metricSource": "nvd@nist.gov", "metricType": "Primary"}, "nReferences": 2, "weaknessAssignment": [{"@type": "WeaknessAssignment", "weakness": [{"@id": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/22.html", "@type": "Weakness", "cweId": "CWE-22", "isInformative": true}], "assignedBy": "134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0", "assignmentType": "Secondary"}, {"@type": "WeaknessAssignment", "weakness": [{"@id": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/22.html", "@type": "Weakness", "cweId": "CWE-22", "isInformative": true}], "assignedBy": "nvd@nist.gov", "assignmentType": "Primary"}], "wasDerivedFrom": ["https://github.com/fkie-cad/nvd-json-data-feeds/tree/a4262227a26a698199ea8d287932f8639e85aa6d"]}, "mappings": [{"@id": "urn:threatgraph:pkev-mapping:1127", "@type": "Mapping", "mappingType": "exploitation_technique", "capabilityGroup": "dir_traversal", "comments": "Due to improper handling of HTTP request input, attackers can exploit a path traversal vulnerability in SimpleHelp version 5.5.7 and prior to gain access to critical user data stored in SimpleHelp, such as credentials. From there, with the credentials, they can further compromise the system, such as with code execution.", "evidenceUrl": ["https://medium.com/@unKnOwn37/simplehelp-cve-2024-57727-tryhackme-3bea119c1c1e"], "wasDerivedFrom": ["https://github.com/center-for-threat-informed-defense/mappings-explorer/tree/ddc842aa48c871cbfc2219cdbb842e9a4e155afe"], "technique": {"@id": "https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1190/", "@type": "AttackTechnique", "techniqueId": "T1190", "name": "Exploit Public-Facing Application", "tactic": [{"@id": "https://attack.mitre.org/tactics/TA0001/", "@type": "AttackTact